--- Whole numbers past 2^53 keep every digit, in both modes: a literal list
--- of them is a list of ints (a tensor, which holds floats, had held
--- 9007199254740993 as ...992), and a parsed list's numbers are walked and
--- encoded as they are (they had been read through a float). A parsed
--- whole number read as a float would lose digits, so it stops; `int[...]`
--- reads it exactly. The last case stops the program.

xs = [9007199254740993, 1]
log[xs[0]]
log[xs[0] + 1]
log[len[xs]]

j = json['[9007199254740993, 2, 2.5]']
for x in j
    log[x]
log[encode[j]]

k = json['{"id": 9007199254740993}']
log[int[k.id]]
log[int[k.id] eq 9007199254740993]

--- read as a float (met in arithmetic): it stops rather than lose digits
log[k.id + 1]
